% Rest of your code here...
\begin{document}

2. Next, add a new command after `\begin{document}` to create the TOC. You may choose any name you like. Here we've used `\tableofcontents`.

   ```
   \maketitle % optional
   \frontmatter % useful for books with front matter
   \tableofcontents
   ```

3. Before compiling the complete document, include the sections you want to appear on the TOC along with their respective headings.

   Use the following syntax to specify a chapter:

   ```latex
      \chapter{Name of Your Chapter here}
     ...Content of Your Chapter goes here
   ```

   Similarly, use these syntax to create other section levels such as subsections, etc.

   ```latex
