     ...Content of Your Section goes here

% if you want subsubsections:
      \subsection{Name of Your Subsection here}
     ...
      \subsubsection{Name of Your Sub-subsection here}
     ...
   ```

4. Finally, compile the entire document using either `pdflatex` or `texlive`. This will create a table of contents that looks similar to this:

   |    |                                                                                                               |
   |:--:|:-------------------------------------------------------|
   | I. | Title of Main Heading                        |
   |   1.| Subtitle of first-level section               |
   |     a.| Subtitle of second-level subsection         |
   |     b.| Subtitle of another second-level subsection |
   |   2.| Subtitle of another first-level section       |
   | II. | Title of Another Main Heading                 |
   |   3.| Subtitle of third-level section               |

Note: This is just an example TOC - it may change based on how you structure headings in your actual document.

Now that you have created the table of contents for your document, whenever you modify or update your files, simply recompile them to reflect any changes you made. The corresponding listing entry will also be adjusted accordingly.

Here's a full example:

```latex
